:''This base has no official name.''
The '''Surge Base''' is an animated [[Enemy Bases|Enemy Base]] that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. It was added in [[Version 9.8 Update|Version 9.8]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Surge Base
|image = E 524.png
|first appearance = '''UL''': [[Happily Ever After|Sub-chapter 27 - Happily Ever After]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Cookie Cutter Ruins|Sub-chapter 12 - Cookie Cutter Ruins]]
|money drop = N/A
}}

==Enemy==
The Surge Base has double the range of the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]] and creates a devastating level 3 [[Surge Attack]] instead of a [[Wave Attack|Wave]]. It deals at least 96,000 damage per hit in all of its appearances, and can spawn Surges between 150 and 2,000 range; a huge area unfortunately paired and evened out in favor of the base as all created Surges have 125 outward piercing range and 250 inner range. Like most animated bases, it is immune to all debuffs and Waves, but can be hurt by Surges and [[Explosion]]s.

While it does use a laser to telegraph ''when'' the Surge is about to go off, it is not possible to determine ''where'' it will occur until it spawns; the aiming laser is cosmetic and always stops in the same area.  Additionally, the Surge Base also has to hit a [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]] in the front with its single-target attack. Beware the telegraph, as you will have only 15 frames (half a second) to prepare before the Surge spawns.

==Strategy==
Because of the Surge Base's extreme damage output, it can easily destroy or cripple whatever it hits, with the Surge lingering on the field for even more carnage. This can be avoided by luring enemies away from its range. Alternatively, you can use [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-Immune units]] such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Beefcake Cat]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr]], although something else is still needed to bait out its attacks.

As mentioned before, the Surge Base is vulnerable to [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attack]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units such as [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], so they could be theoretically useful provided if the Surge Base couldn't eliminate them in time. Apart from the surge, there is also the high damage single-target that hits the enemy in front, so a unit will need to be periodically sent out to intercept it and protect the rushers.

